{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1427647-what-happens-if-you-take-a-photo-inside-the-dreaming","id":1427647,"title":"What happens if you take a photo inside the dreaming?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-07T16:42:20-08:00","id":1427647,"title":"What happens if you take a photo inside the dreaming?","content":"I've been thinking about this lately. and I don't know if the books talks about this directly. <br /> <br /> <br /> I've come up with a few possibilities<br /> <br /> <br /> Old cameras: they take the photos, but since all the information imprinted on the film are chimerical, developing it gets you nothing. (However I wonder which color the develop would be)<br /> However, some changelings might make a method to develop such photos in the real world, but since they are chimerical, only enchanted mortals can see the photos. <br /> <br /> <br /> Polaroid like: Like above, the photo shows it, but only enchanted can see.<br /> <br /> Digital cameras: While you're on the dreaming the photos can be viewed on the camera/cellphone, but once you get in the real world all the information disappear because it was chimerical and don't hold on in the real world. And there is no way to retrive information even for changelings because the kbytes of photos simply disappear once you go through a trod. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Do you think it would work like this? <br /> Also I don't think taking a single photo of something in the dreaming will bring any kinda of banality or cause something negative. But Im wondering if the &quot;cameras capture the soul&quot; might somehow work in a certain way in the dreaming. We know that bunks lose their efficiency if they are used a lot of times, because they are losing the chaos element in them and becoming a set of rules and customs, so bunk need to be fresh. I wonder if taking a lot of photos from a single chimerical place/object in the dreaming might impose banality upon it. Because each photo is one more register of the thing, one more stuff that is proof of how it is. The more photos are taken, the more times the place or thing is registered a single frame, instead of a complex and natural element. Could this make the target more banal? Maybe it don't work in the dreaming because, well, it the dreaming, pure glamour, so banlity can't make a dent in it. But What if it can be used against chiemras or chanelings in the real world? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T13:17:00-08:00","id":1427744,"title":"","content":"I think there\u2019s something to the idea that there could be interesting things done with \u2018cameras capture the soul\u2019 or stuff like Kirlian photography, but I\u2019d also need some time to consider options as what that would look like.<br /> <br /> I would say though that I don\u2019t think you could take a camera into the dreaming without some effort. For one thing it brings into question the state of the physical body of a Changeling within the Dreaming or while they Invoke the Wyrd and what the enchanted brings with them, if an enchanted were brought into the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> I do agree though that if photography can capture chimerical vision then it should only be visible to those able to see chimerically. My question though is if cameras should be able to. My first thought is to rule that they can capture chimerical reality only if that\u2019s the intent of the user, although perhaps particularly strong chimerical bodies can make themselves apparent even to the non-glamour touched. <br /> <br /> I would also agree that limiting the ability to old cameras doesn\u2019t feel quite right. Perhaps it\u2019s easier for old school film to capture things but the right person with the right intent could use a disposable camera or a digital camera if we allow the capturing of chimerical reality through photographs at all. It would depend on the person using the camera\u2019s willingness to accept the possibility for glamour to be captured by the camera I think.<br /> <br /> Ambient banality might also be something worth considering. As in, a picture of a troll exposed to prolonged ambient banality might cause the chimerical image to fade and desaturate like a real photo kept in poor conditions.<br /> <br /> I also think something interesting might be possible with using Harry Potter as a source of inspiration. Photographs of glamour-touched and chimera capture them within a snap shot of that moment, existing within the context of their images, and perhaps even being able to interact with other chimerical images. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s interesting stuff, if one is willing to give it the initial green stamp in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T06:19:39-08:00","id":1427852,"title":"","content":"For the most part, I would say that photos taken in the Dreaming become either too blurry, or appear easily debunked. Much like the &quot;fairy photography&quot; of the Victorian era, it is &quot;clearly&quot; a fake to cynical, modern eyes. At best, such photos might end up on a conspiracy website.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T16:03:44-08:00","id":1428678,"title":"","content":"A reference in the Nocker Kithbook mentions that the Nockers are the only ones that had Video cameras that worked in the dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}